Title: Night Shift
Author: Sample

INT. KITCHEN - NIGHT

Smoke curls under the hood. MIRA, thirties, stirs a pot with her phone pinned to her ear.

The line rings twice, then drops to voicemail.

She hangs up, scrapes the pasta onto a plate, and rinses the pot before she sits down.

INT. LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Mira eats on the floor, back against the couch. Her phone lies face down on the rug.

It buzzes. She doesn't look.

It buzzes again. She answers.

MIRA
You're on speaker.

DAN
(V.O.)
I know. I can hear the echo.

MIRA
You said you'd call back three days ago.

DAN
(V.O.)
I know.

MIRA
So call back.

The clock over the mantel ticks. Mira sets her fork down.

DAN
(V.O.)
I didn't do it.

MIRA
I know.

DAN
(V.O.)
Then why —

MIRA
Because I wanted to hear you say it.

A long pause. The pasta goes cold on her plate.

DAN
(V.O.)
Okay.

MIRA
Okay.

She hangs up. The apartment is very quiet. Then she picks up her fork.
